The setter already compiles to a single inlined store after -O2, so there is no redundant work to remove without risking behavioural changes; I keep it identical to guarantee the checksum and profile sweep match exactly.

```cpp
    void SetMessageIndex(FIT_MESSAGE_INDEX messageIndex)
    {
        SetFieldUINT16Value(254, messageIndex, 0, FIT_SUBFIELD_INDEX_MAIN_FIELD);
    }
```